<!--
  RSW_DurasteelConvert_OuterRim.xml          mandrake.rsw.armoury

  CANON_MATERIALS_BUILD_1 L2 (design section 3.2): OuterRim_Durasteel (Neronix17.OuterRim.Core, workshop 2919227155,
  1.6 + Common folders measured 2026-10-10) is no longer produced; every use of it points at RSW_Durasteel and the
  def is removed. Loose stacks and old saves convert 1:1 through RM_DefAliasDef (alias OuterRim_Durasteel ->
  RSW_Durasteel) rather than the design's conversion recipe: an alias loses nothing and needs no bill. The mod has
  NO mining or deep-drill producer for it in 1.6 (nothing to zero); it appears only in recipe filters/costs, trader
  stock (thingDef), the Binary Star Raiders loot filter and floors (but see the producers below). One Replace per stack count (31 counts today):
  a PatchOperationReplace cannot rename an element and keep its text. The counts were measured in OuterRim.Core only;
  the sister mod neronix17.outerrim.furnitureanddecor spends other counts (its doors, beds, tables, dressers), so a
  final PatchOperationSetName renames EVERY remaining <OuterRim_Durasteel> element to <RSW_Durasteel>, keeping its
  count. Without it those costList entries named the removed def, stayed null, and Minify Everything's Mass-from-costList
  postfix NRE'd on the doors: RimWorld reset ModsConfig to Core (FULL_LIST_LOAD_DIAGNOSE_MINIFY_SAYS_NO, 2026-10-10).
  validation.py (durasteel_outerrim_static) checks the shape, including the catch-all. Every operation is a no-op when the donor is absent.
  Two producers DO name it on the full list (effective_def_lint.py removed_refs, 2026-10-10):
  leutiankane.mineablesor's LKDurasteel_Ore (<mineableThing>) and Ideology's WorkSite_Mining (<thing>), so both
  text forms are rewritten too; without them the ore mined nothing and the work-site entry named a dead def.
-->
